(7430126, 1173834, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that does not meet the challenge<br/> <br/>Whilst it is a very appealing image Drake, I don''t see it as a minimalist image in any way. The focus is nice and clearly defined on this very attractive bird with a shallow DOF to isolate the bird both from the foreground and background. That is where the problem is, there is too much foreground and background for a minimalist shot, if we simply had the bird on 1 twig against a plain sky background then it would be fine. The twigs and foliage are just too much and, interesting as the snow may be, it adds another element where we are seeking the opposite.<br/> <br/>Thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that does not meet the challenge Whilst it is a very appealing image Drake, I don''t see it as a minimalist image in any way. The focus is nice and clearly defined on this very attractive bird with a shallow DOF to isolate the bird both from the foreground and background. That is where the problem is, there is too much foreground and background for a minimalist shot, if we simply had the bird on 1 twig against a plain sky background then it would be fine. The twigs and foliage are just too much and, interesting as the snow may be, it adds another element where we are seeking the opposite. Thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-20 06:33:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7430129, 1173880, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Definitely minimalist! I love your angle of view, as you say, it looks as though its balancing a piece of wire. The composition is good with plenty of negative space, The lighting is good, it reveals the orange''s roundness well, the whiteness of the wire stands out well. The only minor criticism is the bright light of the right of the frame, I think a more uniform background would probably have worked a little better. Generally, a good shot that fulfils the challenge brief very well. <br/> <br/>I''m sorry you didn''t receive any comments during the challenge, I hope this makes up for that. Thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge Definitely minimalist! I love your angle of view, as you say, it looks as though its balancing a piece of wire. The composition is good with plenty of negative space, The lighting is good, it reveals the orange''s roundness well, the whiteness of the wire stands out well. The only minor criticism is the bright light of the right of the frame, I think a more uniform background would probably have worked a little better. Generally, a good shot that fulfils the challenge brief very well.  I''m sorry you didn''t receive any comments during the challenge, I hope this makes up for that. Thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-20 06:42:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7430131, 1173845, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>The way the water and the misty background merge seamlessly into one is what makes this works so well. The composition is good. It is certainly minimalist though any more than what we have would start to lose the feel, in other words there is just enough. A plain post may have been preferable but there was nothing you could do about it at the shooting stage I think it would improve it if the notice were removed.<br/> <br/>I find the exposure way too dark and too low in contrast, I think this would be greatly improved with several stops more exposure to brighten everything up substantially, it would make a great high key shot.<br/> <br/>Thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge The way the water and the misty background merge seamlessly into one is what makes this works so well. The composition is good. It is certainly minimalist though any more than what we have would start to lose the feel, in other words there is just enough. A plain post may have been preferable but there was nothing you could do about it at the shooting stage I think it would improve it if the notice were removed. I find the exposure way too dark and too low in contrast, I think this would be greatly improved with several stops more exposure to brighten everything up substantially, it would make a great high key shot. Thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-20 06:50:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7430133, 1173279, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An amusing image that does not meet the challenge<br/> <br/>Thank you for making me laugh RMP. Your take on the challenges here is always interesting and you are continuing to maintain your high standards here again. What about a suggestion as opposed to your low key approach you could try a high key alternative?<br/> <br/>Thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An amusing image that does not meet the challenge Thank you for making me laugh RMP. Your take on the challenges here is always interesting and you are continuing to maintain your high standards here again. What about a suggestion as opposed to your low key approach you could try a high key alternative? Thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-20 06:56:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7430135, 1173506, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>It certainly fulfils the challenge brief isolated against the plain sky as it is. There appears to be a lot less detail in the bird than I would have expected, it looks as though its been cropped from a much larger image although the lens suggests that this is not the case? There is a lot of noise in the image which is, I suspect, why it has not been as well received by your voters as perhaps you would have expected. I wonder why you used such a small aperture I would have thought f8 would have sufficed which would have enabled you to shoot it at ISO 400 for a much less noisy image. Also as the bird was soaring a slower shutter speed at about 1/1000 would also have sufficed again easing the ISO/noise problem further.<br/> <br/>I think there is a strong argument for significantly increasing the brightness of the sky to raise it to a high key alternative.<br/> <br/>As for the bird, I''m probably wrong but it looks like a herring gull to me. Sorry you didn''t receive any comments during the challenge, I hope this makes up for it. Thank you for your entry.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge It certainly fulfils the challenge brief isolated against the plain sky as it is. There appears to be a lot less detail in the bird than I would have expected, it looks as though its been cropped from a much larger image although the lens suggests that this is not the case? There is a lot of noise in the image which is, I suspect, why it has not been as well received by your voters as perhaps you would have expected. I wonder why you used such a small aperture I would have thought f8 would have sufficed which would have enabled you to shoot it at ISO 400 for a much less noisy image. Also as the bird was soaring a slower shutter speed at about 1/1000 would also have sufficed again easing the ISO/noise problem further. I think there is a strong argument for significantly increasing the brightness of the sky to raise it to a high key alternative. As for the bird, I''m probably wrong but it looks like a herring gull to me. Sorry you didn''t receive any comments during the challenge, I hope this makes up for it. Thank you for your entry.', '2016-01-20 07:08:14.000000', NULL, 0),
